# Pin LF on every platform, including Windows checkouts.
#
# This package publishes with a Sigstore attestation binding the tarball to this
# source, so "the source you read is the code you run" is checkable with
# `npm audit signatures`. That claim is about BYTES. A Windows contributor whose
# checkout converted LF to CRLF commits a file that differs from the one the
# Linux publish job built, for no reason a reader could ever see — which is the
# one failure mode the attestation exists to rule out.
*        text=auto eol=lf
*.tgz    binary
